From cf46a626390ee9555355aeb543610cdea2278bd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: olivergrosche <15156206+olivergrosche@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:40:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: fix minute-long level loads under Wine on Android
 storage

Under Wine (e.g. GameHub or Winlator with FEX) on Android's case-sensitive
FUSE storage, every lookup of a file that does not exist makes Wine scan the
whole directory for a case-insensitive match - about 2-15 ms each on a
Snapdragon tablet, depending on the directory. A savegame load made about
15,000 of them:

- Localize() looks for <package>.int for every translatable property of
  every object it loads (FConfigCacheIni::Find probes with
  GFileManager->FileSize and never remembers a missing file), mostly for
  the map's own .int, which doesn't exist.
- Core tries to load a native DLL for every package it binds:
  <System>\<package>, <System>\<package>.dll and the never valid
  _<System>\<package>.dll.
- appFindPackageFile searches each package in every search path.
- D3D10Drv looks for a replacement .dds under ..\textures for every texture
  it uploads, and for some also .detail.dds and .dds.flags.

PathCache lists each directory below the game directory once and answers
those lookups from the listing; the save and cache directories are never
cached. FileHooks patches the import tables of all loaded modules for the
Win32 file calls: read-only opens and attribute queries of files known to be
missing fail at once with the error the OS would report, and so do Core.dll's
LoadLibraryW calls for package DLLs the listing rules out (and for the never
valid name). Every create, write, move or delete invalidates the affected
directory, and each map load starts with fresh listings. FileSize() is
answered from the listing, and packages are opened by their on-disk spelling.

FastFileReader maps package files into memory (512 MB budget, buffered
fallback) instead of the engine's 1 KB reads with a seek per object.

Diagnostics, off by default: [DeusExe] FileTrace=True logs counts, times and
callers of the file calls per level change, LoadProfiler=True samples the
main thread during map loads. CLevelWatch now also reports a load that
reuses the old level's address or fails. On a crash the hooks pass calls
through.

Measured on the tablet (Proton 11 arm64x + FEX, DXVK): main menu
45.6 s -> 3.1 s (D3D10Drv), savegame load 4-5 min -> 1.1 s (DECoR).
[DeusExe] PathCache=False turns the cache and the hooks off, and
FastFileReader=False uses the engine's reader again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
